# npm audit ignore list, read by scripts/check-npm-audit.sh.
#
# The console's npm audit blocks on HIGH/CRITICAL (decision D2 in
# docs/archive/PROJECT-READINESS-GUIDE.md). An entry here is a claim that one
# advisory does not apply to this repository, which needs a reason a reviewer
# can check, and an exp: date after which it is looked at again.
#
# Do not add an entry to make a build green. Bump the dependency.

# GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm — braces <= 3.0.3, stack exhaustion on deeply nested
# brace patterns. No patched release exists (3.0.3 is the latest braces).
#
# braces is in the tree only through tailwindcss 3 (chokidar and micromatch,
# `npm ls braces`), a devDependency that runs at build time and is not in the
# shipped bundle. The patterns it expands are the `content` globs in
# tailwind.config.js, written in this repository; no request, user or tenant
# input reaches it. The way out is Tailwind 4, which drops chokidar and
# micromatch -- a migration of the console's styling config, tracked as its
# own piece of work rather than smuggled into a CI fix -- or a braces release.
